  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Kummer computation on an affine curve",
  "statement": "Let $k$ be algebraically closed, let $C$ be a\nsmooth affine connected curve over $k$, and let\n$n\\geq1$ be prime to $\\operatorname{char}k$. Then, under the\ncanonical trivialization $\\theta_\\zeta$ of\n[def-sc-mu-trivialization],\n\n$$\nH^0(C_{\\Et},\\mathbf F_n)\\cong\\mathbf Z/n\\mathbf Z,\\qquad\n\\mathcal O_C(C)^\\times/\\mathcal O_C(C)^\\times{}^{\\,n}\n\\text{ is finite},\n$$\n\nand there is a canonical short exact sequence\n\n$$\n0\\longrightarrow\\mathcal O_C(C)^\\times/\\mathcal O_C(C)^\\times{}^{\\,n}\n\\longrightarrow H^1(C_{\\Et},\\mathbf F_n)\\longrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Pic}(C)[n]\\longrightarrow0\n$$\n\n($\\operatorname{Pic}(C)[n]$ finite, by [lem-sc-pic-affine]; the\nunit term vanishes when $\\mathcal O_C(C)^\\times$ is $n$-divisible,\ne.g. when $C=\\mathbf A^1$), and\n$H^q(C_{\\Et},\\mathbf F_n)=0$ for all $q>1$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-cd-affine/thm-sc-affine-cohomology.md",
    "place": "node thm-sc-affine-cohomology, order 1021"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-sc-mu-trivialization",
    "lem-sc-pic-affine",
    "def-sc-curves"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Apply [lem-sc-kummer-les] to the smooth connected affine curve C, using [lem-sc-brauer-zero] for the hypothesis H^2(C, G_m)=0. It gives the canonical short exact sequence 0 → O_C(C)^×/O_C(C)^×ⁿ → H^1(C, μ_n) → Pic(C)[n] → 0 and identifies H^0(C, μ_n) with Z/nZ via [lem-sc-primitive-root]. Transport these groups along the canonical trivialization θ_ζ of [def-sc-mu-trivialization]. The unit quotient is finite by [lem-sc-affine-unit-quotient], while Pic(C)[n] is finite and Pic(C) is n-divisible by [lem-sc-pic-affine]; hence the Kummer H^2 cokernel in [lem-sc-kummer-les] vanishes.",
      "uses": [
        "lem-sc-kummer-les",
        "lem-sc-brauer-zero",
        "lem-sc-primitive-root",
        "def-sc-mu-trivialization",
        "lem-sc-affine-unit-quotient",
        "lem-sc-pic-affine"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The higher-degree vanishing H^q(C_et, F_n)=0 for every q>1 is the affine-curve cohomological-dimension statement [lem-sc-affine-cohomological-dimension], applied to the torsion constant sheaf F_n.",
      "uses": [
        "lem-sc-affine-cohomological-dimension"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
  ],
